course: dictionary
lesson: 10440
title: Truck: one word, many jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A truck is a big vehicle for carrying heavy things. In the UK people often say lorry for the same thing. «You never ride up the inside of a lorry or truck at a junction, because the driver cannot see you and it may turn.» Here lorry and truck mean the same big vehicle.
explain: Truck can also mean other things. A hand truck is a small cart with wheels that you move by pushing. A food truck is a van that cooks and sells food. To work out which one is meant, read the clues: a heavy load means the big vehicle, a cart you push means the hand truck, and cooking and selling food means the food truck.
explain: Big trucks have blind spots, which are places the driver cannot see, even with the mirrors. «The driver of a truck or lorry cannot see a cyclist in its blind spots.» «If you cannot see the driver's face in the truck's mirror, the driver cannot see you either.» So stay well away from a truck, especially when it turns.
explain: Trucks are also used in maths. If each truck carries the same load, the trucks needed is the total divided by the load, rounded up. For 50 boxes and 8 boxes per truck, 50 ÷ 8 = 6 with 2 left over, so you need 7 trucks.
fact: A truck is a big vehicle for carrying heavy things. In the UK it is often called a lorry.
fact: A hand truck is a small cart with wheels that you move by hand.
fact: A food truck is a van that cooks and sells food.
fact: Big trucks have blind spots, places the driver cannot see. Stay far away when they turn.
fact: «Many dumper trucks used on building sites have 6 wheels.»
exercise: «You never ride up the inside of a lorry or truck at a junction.» What is a truck? | A kind of hat | A type of bicycle | A small pet | *A big vehicle for carrying heavy things
exercise: Ella sees a van that cooks and sells hot burgers at the park. What is it called? | A pickup truck | *A food truck | A hand truck | A tow truck
exercise: Why must you stay far away from a truck when it turns? | The driver wants to wave to you | Trucks are slow and quiet | Trucks never turn | *The driver cannot see you in its blind spots
test: Which word means a small cart with wheels that you move by hand? | Dump truck | *Hand truck | Food truck | Fire truck
test: A maths problem: 50 boxes, 8 boxes per truck. How many trucks are needed? | 50 | *7 | 6 | 8
exam: «Many dumper trucks used on building sites have 6 wheels.» How many wheels do many dumper trucks have? | *6 | 8 | 4 | 10
